    {
      "text": "During the spawning season, countless Luvdisc congregate at coral reefs, turning the waters pink.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Luvdisc live in shallow seas in the tropics. This heart-shaped Pokémon earned its name by swimming after loving couples it spotted in the ocean’s waves.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Luvdisc’s heart-shaped body is a symbol of love and romance. It is said that any couple meeting this Pokémon is promised a loving relationship that never ends.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "If a Luvdisc is left on its own, it becomes despondent, leaving itself open to attack. That is when Pelipper snatch them up.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Loving couples have a soft spot for this Pokémon, so honeymoon hotels often release this Pokémon into their pools.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "There was an era when it was overfished due to the rumor that having one of its heart-shaped scales would enable you to find a sweetheart.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Luvdisc makes its home in coral reefs in warm seas. It especially likes sleeping in the space between Corsola’s branches.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    }
  ],
